{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"for f in skills/*/SKILL.md; do printf '%s: ' \\\"\"'$f\"; sed -n '\"'1,8p' \\\"\"'$f\" | tr '\"'\\\\n' ' '; printf '\\\\n'; done\"","aggregated_output":"skills/adversarial/SKILL.md: --- name: adversarial user-invokable: true description: Run a dual-agent adversarial code review. Dispatches a Codex reviewer in parallel with a Claude reviewer. Both review the same diff independently. Surfaces disagreements after both complete. ---  # Adversarial Review  \nskills/dispatch/SKILL.md: --- name: dispatch user-invokable: true description: Run a coding task via darkfactory-dispatch. Accepts a task description inline or prompts for one. Parses the structured JSON result and presents outcome clearly. ---  # Dispatch  \nskills/grill/SKILL.md: --- name: grill user-invokable: true description: Interview the user relentlessly about a plan or design until reaching shared understanding, resolving each branch of the decision tree. Use when user wants to stress-test a plan, get grilled on their design, or mentions \"grill me\". ---  Interview me relentlessly about every aspect of this plan until we reach a shared understanding. Walk down each branch of the design tree, resolving dependencies between decisions one-by-one. For each question, provide your recommended answer.  \nskills/language/SKILL.md: --- name: language user-invokable: true description: Extract a DDD-style ubiquitous language glossary from the current conversation, flagging ambiguities and proposing canonical terms. Saves to UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md. Use when user wants to define domain terms, build a glossary, harden terminology, create a ubiquitous language, or mentions \"domain model\" or \"DDD\". ---  # Ubiquitous Language  \nskills/mission-init/SKILL.md: --- name: mission-init user-invokable: true description: Verify that all Darkfactory skills are installed and required CLI tools are available. Run from any project before starting a mission. ---  # Mission Init  \nskills/mission-resume/SKILL.md: --- name: mission-resume description: Resume an interrupted Darkfactory mission from file state. Finds active missions, reconstructs the orchestrator plan from disk artifacts, detects orphaned commits, and continues the build loop from the next unchecked task. ---  # Mission Resume  Resume a Darkfactory mission that was interrupted (laptop sleep, terminal close, crash, context compaction). All mission state lives on disk. This skill reads it, rebuilds the orchestrator plan, and picks up where the previous session left off. \nskills/mission-status/SKILL.md: --- name: mission-status description: Check the progress of an active Darkfactory mission. Read-only -- does not modify any files. ---  # Mission Status  Show a formatted progress summary for an active Darkfactory mission. This skill is strictly **read-only** -- it MUST NOT create, modify, or delete any files. \nskills/mission/SKILL.md: --- name: mission description: Start an autonomous Darkfactory mission. Grills the user for alignment, creates OpenSpec artifacts, writes a contract, writes the mission directory, dispatches workers serially, validates each task against the contract, runs fix loops with circuit breakers, and creates a draft PR on completion. flow: align -> spec -> contract -> build -> validate -> ship ---  ## Rules (Always Enforced)  \nskills/prd/SKILL.md: --- name: prd user-invokable: true description: Create a PRD through user interview, codebase exploration, and module design, then submit as a GitHub issue. Use when user wants to write a PRD, create a product requirements document, or plan a new feature. ---  This skill will be invoked when the user wants to create a PRD. You may skip steps if you don't consider them necessary.  \nskills/security/SKILL.md: --- name: security user-invokable: true description: Complete a security review of the pending changes on the current branch user_invokable: true globs: [] ---  \nskills/tdd/SKILL.md: --- name: tdd user-invokable: true description: Test-driven development with red-green-refactor loop. Use when user wants to build features or fix bugs using TDD, mentions \"red-green-refactor\", wants integration tests, or asks for test-first development. ---  # Test-Driven Development  \nskills/test-quality/SKILL.md: --- name: test-quality user-invokable: true description: LLM-based semantic review of test effectiveness. Evaluates assertion quality, implementation coupling, branch coverage, behavioral changes without tests, and edge case awareness. Use when scrutiny validator invokes it as a subagent, or when user wants to review test quality independently. ---  # Test Quality Review  \n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
