{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba skills/dispatch/SKILL.md | sed -n '1,240p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t---\n     2\tname: dispatch\n     3\tuser-invokable: true\n     4\tdescription: Run a coding task via darkfactory-dispatch. Accepts a task description inline or prompts for one. Parses the structured JSON result and presents outcome clearly.\n     5\t---\n     6\t\n     7\t# Dispatch\n     8\t\n     9\tRun one coding task through `darkfactory-dispatch` and report the structured result. This is a thin user-facing wrapper around the binary.\n    10\t\n    11\tDo not call the Codex CLI directly. Always use `darkfactory-dispatch`.\n    12\t\n    13\t## Input\n    14\t\n    15\tAccept the task description in either mode:\n    16\t\n    17\t- Inline: `/dispatch Fix the failing auth tests in src/auth.test.ts`\n    18\t- No argument: ask the user `What task should I dispatch?` and wait for their description.\n    19\t\n    20\tIf the final task description is empty, stop and ask again.\n    21\t\n    22\t## Step 1: Write A Prompt File\n    23\t\n    24\tWrite the task description to a temp file:\n    25\t\n    26\t```bash\n    27\tPROMPT_PATH=$(mktemp /tmp/dispatch-task.XXXXXX)\n    28\tcat > \"$PROMPT_PATH\" << 'TASK'\n    29\t<task description>\n    30\tTASK\n    31\t```\n    32\t\n    33\t## Step 2: Run darkfactory-dispatch\n    34\t\n    35\tRun the dispatcher from the current project directory and request structured JSON output:\n    36\t\n    37\t```bash\n    38\tdarkfactory-dispatch \\\n    39\t  --model gpt-5.5 \\\n    40\t  --effort high \\\n    41\t  --timeout 1800 \\\n    42\t  --sandbox workspace-write \\\n    43\t  --config 'sandbox_workspace_write.writable_roots=[\".git\"]' \\\n    44\t  --prompt-file \"$PROMPT_PATH\" \\\n    45\t  --cwd \"$(pwd)\" \\\n    46\t  --json\n    47\t```\n    48\t\n    49\tCapture stdout. Parse the JSON result with `jq`.\n    50\t\n    51\tUseful fields:\n    52\t\n    53\t- `.status`\n    54\t- `.duration_ms`\n    55\t- `.activity.files_changed`\n    56\t- `.output`\n    57\t- `.error.message`\n    58\t- `.log`\n    59\t\n    60\tAlways remove the temp prompt file after dispatch completes or fails:\n    61\t\n    62\t```bash\n    63\trm -f \"$PROMPT_PATH\"\n    64\t```\n    65\t\n    66\t## Step 3: Present Outcome\n    67\t\n    68\tIf `.status` is `completed`, present:\n    69\t\n    70\t```text\n    71\tDispatch complete.\n    72\t\n    73\tStatus: completed\n    74\tDuration: <elapsed time>\n    75\tFiles written: <list from result, or \"none reported\">\n    76\tOutput: <output path if --output was set, otherwise \"see above\">\n    77\t```\n    78\t\n    79\tFor files written, use `.activity.files_changed` when it exists and is non-empty. Otherwise write `none reported`.\n    80\t\n    81\tFor duration, prefer a human-readable value derived from `.duration_ms`.\n    82\t\n    83\tFor output, use `.output` when present and non-empty. Otherwise write `see above`.\n    84\t\n    85\tIf `.status` is `failed`, `.status` is `timed_out`, the command exits non-zero, JSON parsing fails, or any other error occurs, present:\n    86\t\n    87\t```text\n    88\tDispatch failed.\n    89\t\n    90\tStatus: <status>\n    91\tError: <error.message from JSON, or \"no error message\">\n    92\tLog: <log path if available>\n    93\t\n    94\tThe task did not complete. Review the error above and retry or adjust the task description.\n    95\t```\n    96\t\n    97\tDo not suppress failures. Always show the error clearly.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
