{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba skills/adversarial/SKILL.md | sed -n '1,260p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t---\n     2\tname: adversarial\n     3\tuser-invokable: true\n     4\tdescription: Run a dual-agent adversarial code review. Dispatches a Codex reviewer in parallel with a Claude reviewer. Both review the same diff independently. Surfaces disagreements after both complete.\n     5\t---\n     6\t\n     7\t# Adversarial Review\n     8\t\n     9\tRun two independent reviewers against the same diff, then compare their reports. This skill is standalone and does not depend on the mission system.\n    10\t\n    11\t## Input Modes\n    12\t\n    13\tDetermine the mode from the optional argument:\n    14\t\n    15\t- No argument: review `git diff HEAD` for all staged and unstaged working tree changes.\n    16\t- PR number, such as `/adversarial 42`: review `gh pr diff 42`.\n    17\t- File path, such as `/adversarial path/to/file.ts`: review `git diff HEAD -- path/to/file.ts`.\n    18\t\n    19\tTreat an all-digit argument as a PR number. Treat any other non-empty argument as a file path.\n    20\t\n    21\t## Report Paths\n    22\t\n    23\tBefore dispatching reviewers, choose report paths:\n    24\t\n    25\t- If the repo contains a Darkfactory mission directory matching `openspec/changes/*/mission/`, write reports under that mission:\n    26\t  - `mission/validations/adversarial-codex.md`\n    27\t  - `mission/validations/adversarial-claude.md`\n    28\t- Otherwise, write reports to temp files and tell the user both paths:\n    29\t  - `/tmp/adversarial-codex-<timestamp>.md`\n    30\t  - `/tmp/adversarial-claude-<timestamp>.md`\n    31\t\n    32\tWhen a mission path is used, create `mission/validations/` if needed.\n    33\t\n    34\t## Step 1: Get The Diff\n    35\t\n    36\tRun exactly one diff command based on the input mode:\n    37\t\n    38\t```bash\n    39\tgit diff HEAD\n    40\tgh pr diff <number>\n    41\tgit diff HEAD -- <path>\n    42\t```\n    43\t\n    44\tIf the diff is empty, report `No changes to review` and stop.\n    45\t\n    46\tSave the diff content once and pass the identical content to both reviewers.\n    47\t\n    48\t## Step 2: Dispatch Codex Reviewer\n    49\t\n    50\tStart Codex first and do not wait for it before launching Claude. Dispatch with `darkfactory-dispatch --async` and use the Bash tool with `run_in_background: true`.\n    51\t\n    52\tPrompt:\n    53\t\n    54\t```text\n    55\tYou are an adversarial code reviewer. Review the following diff for bugs, logic errors, security issues, and missing edge cases. Group findings by severity: critical, warning, nit. Cite file:line for each finding. Write your report to: <codex-report-path>\n    56\t\n    57\t<diff content>\n    58\t```\n    59\t\n    60\tDispatch command:\n    61\t\n    62\t```bash\n    63\tPROMPT_PATH=$(mktemp /tmp/adversarial-prompt.XXXXXX)\n    64\tcat > \"$PROMPT_PATH\" << 'PROMPT'\n    65\tYou are an adversarial code reviewer. Review the following diff for bugs, logic errors, security issues, and missing edge cases. Group findings by severity: critical, warning, nit. Cite file:line for each finding. Write your report to: <codex-report-path>\n    66\t\n    67\t<diff content>\n    68\tPROMPT\n    69\t\n    70\tdarkfactory-dispatch \\\n    71\t  --async \\\n    72\t  --model gpt-5.5 \\\n    73\t  --effort high \\\n    74\t  --timeout 900 \\\n    75\t  --sandbox workspace-write \\\n    76\t  --prompt-file \"$PROMPT_PATH\" \\\n    77\t  --output \"<codex-report-path>\" \\\n    78\t  --cwd \"$(pwd)\" \\\n    79\t  --json\n    80\t```\n    81\t\n    82\t## Step 3: Dispatch Claude Reviewer\n    83\t\n    84\tWhile Codex is running in the background, dispatch Claude via the Agent tool. Give Claude the same diff content and the same reviewer prompt, changing only the report path to `<claude-report-path>`.\n    85\t\n    86\tClaude must write its report to `adversarial-claude.md` at the selected report path.\n    87\t\n    88\t## Step 4: Collect Results\n    89\t\n    90\tAfter Claude finishes, wait for the background Codex dispatch to complete. Then read both report files.\n    91\t\n    92\tFor each report, count findings by severity:\n    93\t\n    94\t- `critical`\n    95\t- `warning`\n    96\t- `nit`\n    97\t\n    98\tFind disagreements:\n    99\t\n   100\t- Findings that appear in the Codex report but not the Claude report.\n   101\t- Findings that appear in the Claude report but not the Codex report.\n   102\t- Findings both report but classify with different severity.\n   103\t\n   104\tCompare findings by affected file, line, and issue description. Minor wording differences do not count as a disagreement when the same bug is clearly being described.\n   105\t\n   106\t## User Output\n   107\t\n   108\tPresent the final result in this format:\n   109\t\n   110\t```text\n   111\tAdversarial review complete.\n   112\t\n   113\tCodex reviewer: N critical, M warnings, P nits\n   114\t  Full report: <path>\n   115\t\n   116\tClaude reviewer: N critical, M warnings, P nits\n   117\t  Full report: <path>\n   118\t\n   119\tDisagreements (flagged by one reviewer only):\n   120\t- [Codex only] <finding>\n   121\t- [Claude only] <finding>\n   122\t\n   123\tReview the full reports and decide what to address.\n   124\t```\n   125\t\n   126\tIf there are no disagreements, write:\n   127\t\n   128\t```text\n   129\tDisagreements (flagged by one reviewer only):\n   130\t- None\n   131\t```\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
