{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba skills/mission-init/SKILL.md | sed -n '1,260p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t---\n     2\tname: mission-init\n     3\tuser-invokable: true\n     4\tdescription: Verify that all Darkfactory skills are installed and required CLI tools are available. Run from any project before starting a mission.\n     5\t---\n     6\t\n     7\t# Mission Init\n     8\t\n     9\tVerify the current project is ready to run `/mission`. Check skill symlinks, initialize OpenSpec if needed, verify required CLI tools, detect the coverage tool, and print one setup report.\n    10\t\n    11\t## Step 1: Check Skill Symlinks\n    12\t\n    13\tCheck these 12 owned skills:\n    14\t\n    15\t```bash\n    16\tmission mission-resume mission-status mission-init grill prd language tdd test-quality security adversarial dispatch\n    17\t```\n    18\t\n    19\tFor each skill, verify:\n    20\t\n    21\t1. `$HOME/.claude/skills/<name>` exists as a symlink, not a regular file or directory.\n    22\t2. The symlink target exists.\n    23\t3. `readlink \"$HOME/.claude/skills/<name>\"` equals `$HOME/.darkfactory/skills/<name>`.\n    24\t\n    25\tUse this status format:\n    26\t\n    27\t```text\n    28\t  [x] /mission - symlink OK\n    29\t  [ ] /adversarial - missing (symlink does not exist)\n    30\t  [!] /dispatch - broken (symlink exists but target missing)\n    31\t  [!] /prd - wrong target\n    32\t```\n    33\t\n    34\tUse a Bash pattern that always exits 0:\n    35\t\n    36\t```bash\n    37\tfor skill in mission mission-resume mission-status mission-init grill prd language tdd test-quality security adversarial dispatch; do\n    38\t  link=\"$HOME/.claude/skills/$skill\"\n    39\t  expected=\"$HOME/.darkfactory/skills/$skill\"\n    40\t\n    41\t  if [ ! -L \"$link\" ]; then\n    42\t    echo \"[ ] /$skill - missing (symlink does not exist)\"\n    43\t  elif [ ! -e \"$link\" ]; then\n    44\t    echo \"[!] /$skill - broken (symlink exists but target missing)\"\n    45\t  else\n    46\t    target=\"$(readlink \"$link\" 2>/dev/null || true)\"\n    47\t    if [ \"$target\" != \"$expected\" ]; then\n    48\t      echo \"[!] /$skill - wrong target\"\n    49\t    else\n    50\t      echo \"[x] /$skill - symlink OK\"\n    51\t    fi\n    52\t  fi\n    53\tdone\n    54\t```\n    55\t\n    56\tIf any required skill is missing, broken, or points to the wrong target, instruct the user to run:\n    57\t\n    58\t```bash\n    59\t~/.darkfactory/install.sh\n    60\t```\n    61\t\n    62\tThen tell them to restart Claude Code and re-run `/mission-init`. Stop after reporting the missing skill fixes.\n    63\t\n    64\tIf all 12 skills are present and resolve correctly, report:\n    65\t\n    66\t```text\n    67\tAll 12 skills: OK\n    68\t```\n    69\t\n    70\tThen continue.\n    71\t\n    72\t## Step 2: Initialize OpenSpec\n    73\t\n    74\tCheck for `openspec/config.yaml` in the current directory.\n    75\t\n    76\tIf it exists, report:\n    77\t\n    78\t```text\n    79\tOpenSpec: already initialized.\n    80\t```\n    81\t\n    82\tIf it does not exist, first check whether the `openspec` CLI is available:\n    83\t\n    84\t```bash\n    85\topenspec --version 2>/dev/null || echo \"NOT_INSTALLED\"\n    86\t```\n    87\t\n    88\tIf `openspec` is not installed, report:\n    89\t\n    90\t```text\n    91\tOpenSpec CLI not installed. Run: `npm install -g @fission-ai/openspec`\n    92\t```\n    93\t\n    94\tIf it is installed, run:\n    95\t\n    96\t```bash\n    97\topenspec init --tools claude,codex --force\n    98\t```\n    99\t\n   100\tAfter a first-time init, tell the user to restart Claude Code so `/opsx:` commands can register.\n   101\t\n   102\t## Step 3: Verify CLI Dependencies\n   103\t\n   104\tRun these checks. Each command must always exit 0 so parallel Bash calls do not cancel each other:\n   105\t\n   106\t```bash\n   107\tcodex --version 2>/dev/null || echo \"NOT_INSTALLED\"\n   108\tdarkfactory-dispatch --version 2>/dev/null || echo \"NOT_INSTALLED\"\n   109\tgh --version 2>/dev/null || echo \"NOT_INSTALLED\"\n   110\tgh auth status 2>/dev/null || echo \"NOT_INSTALLED\"\n   111\topenspec --version 2>/dev/null || echo \"NOT_INSTALLED\"\n   112\tjq --version 2>/dev/null || echo \"NOT_INSTALLED\"\n   113\t```\n   114\t\n   115\tReport each tool as installed, not installed, or not authenticated.\n   116\t\n   117\t- `codex`: if missing, fix with `npm install -g @openai/codex`. If installed but a Codex command reports an auth failure, fix with `codex login`.\n   118\t- `darkfactory-dispatch`: if missing, fix with `cd ~/.darkfactory/tools/darkfactory-dispatch && make install`.\n   119\t- `gh`: if `gh --version` is missing, fix with `brew install gh`. If `gh auth status` fails while `gh` is installed, fix with `gh auth login`.\n   120\t- `openspec`: if missing, fix with `npm install -g @fission-ai/openspec`.\n   121\t- `jq`: if missing, fix with `brew install jq`.\n   122\t\n   123\t## Step 4: Coverage Tool Detection\n   124\t\n   125\tDetect the project language from build files at the project root:\n   126\t\n   127\t- `Cargo.toml` means Rust.\n   128\t- `package.json` means TypeScript/Node.\n   129\t- `pyproject.toml` or `requirements.txt` means Python.\n   130\t\n   131\tCheck the matching coverage tool.\n   132\t\n   133\tFor Rust:\n   134\t\n   135\t```bash\n   136\tcargo tarpaulin --version 2>/dev/null || echo \"NOT_INSTALLED\"\n   137\t```\n   138\t\n   139\tIf missing, suggest:\n   140\t\n   141\t```bash\n   142\tcargo install cargo-tarpaulin\n   143\t```\n   144\t\n   145\tFor TypeScript/Node, check `package.json` for `c8`, `jest`, or `istanbul` in `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Use an exit-0 pattern:\n   146\t\n   147\t```bash\n   148\tnode -e 'const p=require(\"./package.json\"); const d={...(p.dependencies||{}), ...(p.devDependencies||{})}; console.log([\"c8\",\"jest\",\"istanbul\"].some((k)=>d[k]) ? \"FOUND\" : \"NOT_INSTALLED\")' 2>/dev/null || echo \"NOT_INSTALLED\"\n   149\t```\n   150\t\n   151\tIf missing, suggest:\n   152\t\n   153\t```bash\n   154\tnpm install -D c8\n   155\t```\n   156\t\n   157\tFor Python:\n   158\t\n   159\t```bash\n   160\tpip show pytest-cov 2>/dev/null || echo \"NOT_INSTALLED\"\n   161\t```\n   162\t\n   163\tIf missing, suggest:\n   164\t\n   165\t```bash\n   166\tpip install pytest-cov\n   167\t```\n   168\t\n   169\tIf no recognized build file exists, report:\n   170\t\n   171\t```text\n   172\tNo recognized language detected - coverage tool check skipped.\n   173\t```\n   174\t\n   175\t## Step 5: Report Status\n   176\t\n   177\tPrint a structured report:\n   178\t\n   179\t```text\n   180\tDarkfactory Setup Report\n   181\t========================\n   182\t\n   183\tSkills (via ~/.claude/skills/ symlinks):\n   184\t  [x] /mission\n   185\t  [x] /mission-resume\n   186\t  [x] /mission-status\n   187\t  [x] /mission-init\n   188\t  [x] /grill\n   189\t  [x] /prd\n   190\t  [x] /language\n   191\t  [x] /tdd\n   192\t  [x] /test-quality\n   193\t  [x] /security\n   194\t  [x] /adversarial\n   195\t  [x] /dispatch\n   196\t\n   197\tOptional project skills:\n   198\t  [ ] /test-app (optional - project-specific)\n   199\t  [ ] /demo-video (optional - project-specific)\n   200\t\n   201\tCLI tools:\n   202\t  [x] codex (authenticated)\n   203\t  [x] darkfactory-dispatch\n   204\t  [x] gh (authenticated)\n   205\t  [x] openspec\n   206\t  [x] jq\n   207\t\n   208\tCoverage:\n   209\t  [x] cargo-tarpaulin (Rust detected)\n   210\t\n   211\tOpenSpec:\n   212\t  [x] Initialized\n   213\t\n   214\tReady: run /mission to start.\n   215\t```\n   216\t\n   217\tAlso check optional project skills at these locations:\n   218\t\n   219\t- `$HOME/.claude/skills/test-app`\n   220\t- `$HOME/.claude/skills/demo-video`\n   221\t- `.claude/skills/test-app`\n   222\t- `.claude/skills/demo-video`\n   223\t\n   224\tOptional skills never block 