{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba skills/security/SKILL.md | sed -n '1,260p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t---\n     2\tname: security\n     3\tuser-invokable: true\n     4\tdescription: Complete a security review of the pending changes on the current branch\n     5\tuser_invokable: true\n     6\tglobs: []\n     7\t---\n     8\t\n     9\t# Security Review\n    10\tWork through each section. Report findings using the output format at the end.\n    11\t\n    12\t## Authorization (IDOR)\n    13\tCheck every endpoint that takes an ID parameter. Verify the user can access that specific resource.\n    14\t**Pattern to flag** - auth check without ownership check:\n    15\t```typescript\n    16\tconst post = await db.posts.findUnique({ where: { id: req.params.id } })\n    17\treturn res.json(post) // Any user can access any post\n    18\t// Fixed\n    19\tconst post = await db.posts.findUnique({ where: { id: req.params.id } })\n    20\tif (post.authorId !== req.user.id) return res.status(403)\n    21\t```\n    22\tCheck for:\n    23\t- Endpoints that fetch by ID without filtering by user/org\n    24\t- Update/delete operations missing ownership verification\n    25\t- Multi-tenant data leaking across organizations\n    26\t- API keys granting access beyond their owner's resources\n    27\t\n    28\t## Input Validation\n    29\tCheck that user input is validated at API boundaries using Zod or similar.\n    30\t**Pattern to flag** - using req.body directly:\n    31\t```typescript\n    32\tawait db.posts.create({ data: req.body }) // Unvalidated\n    33\t// Fixed\n    34\tconst data = CreatePostSchema.parse(req.body)\n    35\tawait db.posts.create({ data })\n    36\t```\n    37\tAlso validate URL params and query strings, not just request bodies.\n    38\t\n    39\t## Environment Variables\n    40\tCheck for:\n    41\t- Hardcoded secrets in source code\n    42\t- Secrets in client-exposed variables (`NEXT_PUBLIC_*`, `VITE_*`, etc.)\n    43\t- Missing `.env` in `.gitignore`\n    44\t- No startup validation of required env vars\n    45\t\n    46\t## Injection\n    47\t**SQL/NoSQL** - flag string interpolation in queries:\n    48\t```typescript\n    49\tdb.query(`SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ${userId}`) // Vulnerable\n    50\tdb.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1', [userId]) // Safe\n    51\t```\n    52\t**XSS** - flag these patterns:\n    53\t- `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with user content\n    54\t- `element.innerHTML = userInput`\n    55\t- `href={userInput}` (javascript: URLs execute)\n    56\t**Command injection** - flag `exec()` with interpolation:\n    57\t```typescript\n    58\texec(`convert ${filename} output.png`) // Vulnerable\n    59\texecFile('convert', [filename, 'output.png']) // Safe\n    60\t```\n    61\t**Template injection** - flag user input in template engines:\n    62\t```typescript\n    63\tconst html = ejs.render(userTemplate); // Vulnerable\n    64\tconst html = ejs.render(staticTemplate, { data: userData }); // Safe\n    65\t```\n    66\t**Unvalidated redirects** - flag redirects using user input:\n    67\t```typescript\n    68\tres.redirect(req.query.next); // Vulnerable - open redirect\n    69\tconst allowed = ['/', '/dashboard', '/profile'];\n    70\tif (allowed.includes(req.query.next)) res.redirect(req.query.next); // Safe\n    71\t```\n    72\t**File uploads**:\n    73\t- Missing file type validation (check magic bytes, not just extension)\n    74\t- No file size limits\n    75\t- Uploaded files served from same domain (enables XSS)\n    76\t- Path traversal in filenames (`../../etc/passwd`)\n    77\t\n    78\t## Secrets\n    79\tFlag:\n    80\t- API keys, passwords, tokens in source code\n    81\t- `console.log(req.body)` that may log credentials\n    82\t- Secrets in error messages returned to clients\n    83\t- Tokens without expiration\n    84\t\n    85\t## Data Protection\n    86\tCheck for:\n    87\t- Plaintext storage of sensitive data (PII, credentials)\n    88\t- Weak encryption algorithms (DES, RC4, ECB mode)\n    89\t- Hardcoded encryption keys\n    90\t- Full credit card/SSN in API responses (mask to last 4 digits)\n    91\t- Verbose error messages exposing stack traces or DB schema\n    92\t- PII logged without redaction\n    93\t- PII in URLs or query strings\n    94\t\n    95\t## Authentication & Sessions\n    96\tCheck for:\n    97\t- Missing auth middleware on protected routes\n    98\t- `Math.random()` for tokens (use `crypto.randomBytes` or `crypto.randomUUID`)\n    99\t- Cookies missing `httpOnly`, `secure`, or `sameSite` flags\n   100\t- JWT tokens without expiration\n   101\t- No rate limiting on login/password reset endpoints\n   102\t- Passwords stored with weak hashing (MD5, SHA1) -- use bcrypt/argon2\n   103\t- Session ID not regenerated after login (session fixation)\n   104\t- No account lockout after failed attempts\n   105\t\n   106\t## Race Conditions\n   107\tFlag check-then-act patterns in financial/inventory operations:\n   108\t```typescript\n   109\t// Vulnerable - race between check and deduct\n   110\tconst balance = await getBalance(userId)\n   111\tif (balance >= amount) await deductBalance(userId, amount)\n   112\t// Safe - atomic transaction\n   113\tawait db.transaction(async (tx) => {\n   114\t  const balance = await tx.getBalance(userId, { forUpdate: true })\n   115\t  if (balance < amount) throw new Error('Insufficient funds')\n   116\t  await tx.deductBalance(userId, amount)\n   117\t})\n   118\t```\n   119\t\n   120\t## Security Headers\n   121\tCheck that the app configures:\n   122\t- `Strict-Transport-Security` (HSTS)\n   123\t- `Content-Security-Policy`\n   124\t- `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`\n   125\t- `X-Frame-Options: DENY` or CSP `frame-ancestors`\n   126\t- `Referrer-Policy`\n   127\t- `Permissions-Policy`\n   128\t\n   129\t## CSRF Protection\n   130\tCheck for:\n   131\t- Missing CSRF tokens on state-changing operations\n   132\t- CSRF tokens not validated server-side\n   133\tFor SPAs: Use `SameSite=Strict` cookies + custom headers (e.g., `X-Requested-With`).\n   134\t\n   135\t## CORS Configuration\n   136\tFlag overly permissive CORS:\n   137\t```typescript\n   138\tapp.use(cors({ origin: '*', credentials: true })); // Vulnerable\n   139\tapp.use(cors({\n   140\t  origin: ['https://app.example.com'],\n   141\t  credentials: true,\n   142\t  methods: ['GET', 'POST'],\n   143\t})); // Safe\n   144\t```\n   145\tCheck for `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` with credentials.\n   146\t\n   147\t## API Security\n   148\tFlag:\n   149\t- Stack traces in production error responses\n   150\t- Database error messages exposed to clients\n   151\t- Sensitive operations on GET requests\n   152\t- GraphQL introspection enabled in production\n   153\t- Swagger/OpenAPI docs exposed without auth\n   154\t- Admin endpoints without additional auth layer\n   155\t- Batch endpoints without limits\n   156\t\n   157\t## Client-Side Security\n   158\tFlag:\n   159\t- Unsafe DOM manipulation (`innerHTML`, `document.write` with user input)\n   160\t- Missing origin validation on `postMessage`\n   161\t- Sensitive data in `localStorage`/`sessionStorage`\n   162\t- External scripts without subresource integrity (SRI) hashes\n   163\t- iframes from untrusted sources without `sandbox` attribute\n   164\t- Webhook endpoints without signature verification\n   165\t\n   166\t## Infrastructure & Configuration\n   167\tCheck for:\n   168\t- Default credentials on any service\n   169\t- Debug mode enabled in production\n   170\t- Source maps deployed to production\n   171\t- `.git` directory exposed in web root\n   172\t- TLS versions below 1.2\n   173\t- `NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED = '0'` in production\n   174\t- Test accounts or backdoors in production code\n   175\t\n   176\t## Dependencies\n   177\tIf reviewing changes to package manifests or lock files:\n   178\t- Run `npm audit --audit-level=high` (or equivalent)\n   179\t- Flag outdated packages with known CVEs\n   180\t- Check for dependency confusion risk (private names conflicting with public registry)\n   181\t- Verify lockfile is committed with integrity hashes\n   182\t\n   183\t## Post-Review Checks\n   184\tAfter completing the review, run:\n   185\t```bash\n   186\t# Dependency audit\n   187\tnpm audit --audit-level=high 2>/dev/null || pnpm audit 2>/dev/null || true\n   188\t# Secret scanning\n   189\tgrep -rE \"(api[_-]?key|secret|token|password)\\s*[:=]\\s*['\\\"][^'\\\"]+['\\\"]\" --include=\"*.ts\" --include=\"*.js\" --include=\"*.py\" --include=\"*.go\" || true\n   190\tgrep -rE \"AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}\" --include=\"*.ts\" --include=\"*.js\" --include=\"*.py\" --include=\"*.go\" || true\n   191\t```\n   192\t\n   193\t## Output Format\n   194\t```\n   195\t## Critical\n   196\t- `src/api/posts.ts:23` - IDOR: delete endpoint missing ownership check\n   197\t- `src/lib/db.ts:45` - SQL injection via string interpolation\n   198\t## High\n   199\t- `src/api/auth.ts:12` - No rate limiting on login endpoint\n   200\t- `.env` - Not in .gitignore\n   201\t## Medium\n   202\t- `src/helpers.ts:23` - Unpinned package versions\n   203\t- `src/ws.ts:112` - Session token in URL query params\n   204\t```\n   205\tUse `file:line` format. State the issue concisely.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
