{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba skills/mission/SKILL.md | sed -n '700,830p'\"","aggregated_output":"   700\t\n   701\tLog the human's decision for each discrepancy to progress.md.\n   702\t\n   703\t### Create Draft PR\n   704\t\n   705\tCreate a **draft** pull request using `gh pr create --draft`. Never create a ready-for-review PR. Use the PR body template below. The `Closes #<N>` directive in the PR body will auto-close the PRD issue when the PR merges.\n   706\t\n   707\t#### PR Body Template\n   708\t\n   709\tRead [templates/pr-body.md](templates/pr-body.md) and fill in the values.\n   710\t\n   711\tSince the PR is created as a draft, the issue stays open until the developer promotes and merges the PR.\n   712\t\n   713\t### Dual Adversarial Review\n   714\t\n   715\tAfter the draft PR is created, run a final adversarial review that walks every mission commit one at a time, groups findings by task, and does a final cross-task pass. Reviewers do not read the full diff in one go -- that stalls on large missions. The per-commit loop keeps each read bounded.\n   716\t\n   717\tRun two independent reviewers in parallel:\n   718\t- **Reviewer A** (engine from `adversarial_reviewer_a` in config.yaml, default: codex) -- dispatched via Bash with `run_in_background: true`\n   719\t- **Reviewer B** (engine from `adversarial_reviewer_b` in config.yaml, default: claude) -- dispatched via Agent tool\n   720\t\n   721\tBoth receive a **pinned base SHA** (the merge-base of `<base-branch>` and HEAD, resolved once up front), the full contract.md, and the report path. The prompt instructs each reviewer to run `git log --reverse --format=\"%h %s\" <base-sha>..HEAD` itself and iterate. Pinning avoids the review scope shifting if `<base-branch>` moves during the review.\n   722\t\n   723\tBefore dispatching either reviewer, compute the base SHA:\n   724\t\n   725\t```bash\n   726\tBASE_SHA=$(git merge-base <base-branch> HEAD)\n   727\tif [ -z \"$BASE_SHA\" ]; then\n   728\t  echo \"ABORT: could not resolve merge-base for <base-branch>..HEAD\"\n   729\t  exit 1\n   730\tfi\n   731\t```\n   732\t\n   733\tPass `$BASE_SHA` into both reviewer prompts.\n   734\t\n   735\t#### Adversarial Reviewer Prompt (used for both A and B)\n   736\t\n   737\tRead [prompts/adversarial-reviewer.md](prompts/adversarial-reviewer.md) and use it as the subagent prompt. Fill in the base SHA (from `$BASE_SHA` above), the full contract.md content, and the absolute report path.\n   738\t\n   739\t#### Reviewer A Dispatch Script (codex)\n   740\t\n   741\t```bash\n   742\tREPORT_PATH=\"<absolute path to mission/validations/adversarial-a.md>\"\n   743\tLOG_PATH=\"<absolute path to mission/logs/adversarial-a-codex.log>\"\n   744\tPROMPT_PATH=$(mktemp /tmp/mission-prompt.XXXXXX)\n   745\t\n   746\t# Guard mission-prompt* from the stale temp cleanup\n   747\tfind /tmp -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 -user \"$(whoami)\" -mmin +30 -not -name \"claude-*\" -not -name \"*mission-prompt*\" \\( -type f -delete -o -type d -exec rm -rf {} + \\) 2>/dev/null\n   748\t\n   749\t# Write the adversarial-reviewer.md prompt content to $PROMPT_PATH with $BASE_SHA, contract.md content, and report path filled in\n   750\t\n   751\t# Dispatch via darkfactory-dispatch: process supervisor with timeout, heartbeat, and structured JSON result\n   752\tDISPATCH_RESULT=$(darkfactory-dispatch \\\n   753\t  --model gpt-5.5 \\\n   754\t  --effort high \\\n   755\t  --timeout 2700 \\\n   756\t  --sandbox workspace-write \\\n   757\t  --prompt-file \"$PROMPT_PATH\" \\\n   758\t  --output \"$REPORT_PATH\" \\\n   759\t  --cwd \"$(pwd)\" \\\n   760\t  --log \"$LOG_PATH\" \\\n   761\t  --json 2>>\"$LOG_PATH\")\n   762\t\n   763\trm -f \"$PROMPT_PATH\"\n   764\t\n   765\tif [ -z \"$DISPATCH_RESULT\" ]; then\n   766\t  echo \"REVIEW_FAILED: dispatcher crashed with no output. Log: $LOG_PATH\"\n   767\telse\n   768\t  DISPATCH_STATUS=$(echo \"$DISPATCH_RESULT\" | jq -r '.status')\n   769\t  DISPATCH_ERROR=$(echo \"$DISPATCH_RESULT\" | jq -r '.error.message // empty')\n   770\t\n   771\t  if [ \"$DISPATCH_STATUS\" = \"completed\" ] && [ -f \"$REPORT_PATH\" ]; then\n   772\t    echo \"REVIEW_COMPLETE: report written\"\n   773\t  else\n   774\t    echo \"REVIEW_FAILED: dispatch status $DISPATCH_STATUS${DISPATCH_ERROR:+; error: $DISPATCH_ERROR}; report $([ -f \"$REPORT_PATH\" ] && echo present || echo missing). Log: $LOG_PATH\"\n   775\t  fi\n   776\tfi\n   777\t```\n   778\t\n   779\tThe Bash tool returns a shell task ID immediately. Reviewer B runs synchronously via the Agent tool. To run them in parallel: **dispatch Reviewer A first** (non-blocking, returns a shell task ID), **then dispatch Reviewer B** (blocks until it returns). When B returns, call BashOutput on A's shell task ID -- if A is done, the final line is `REVIEW_COMPLETE` or `REVIEW_FAILED`; if not, wait for A's completion notification before reading.\n   780\t\n   781\t**Human visibility:** To watch Reviewer A progress live, run `tail -f <absolute path to mission/logs/adversarial-a-codex.log>` in another terminal.\n   782\t\n   783\t### Present to Human\n   784\t\n   785\tLog to progress.md: `<timestamp> -- Draft PR created: <URL>. Adversarial reviews complete.`\n   786\t\n   787\tRead `mission/fallbacks.log` if it exists. If it contains entries, build the fallback summary section. If the file does not exist or is empty, omit the section entirely.\n   788\t\n   789\tPresent the results to the user:\n   790\t\n   791\t```\n   792\tMission complete.\n   793\t\n   794\tDraft PR: <URL>\n   795\t\n   796\t[Only if mission/fallbacks.log has entries:]\n   797\tCodex Fallback Summary:\n   798\t- <count> of <total tasks> tasks required Claude fallback:\n   799\t  - Task N: <reason> (<task-name>)\n   800\t  - Task M: <reason> (<task-name>)\n   801\t\n   802\tAdversarial Review A (Codex):\n   803\t<summary of findings -- count by severity>\n   804\t\n   805\tAdversarial Review B (Claude):\n   806\t<summary of findings -- count by severity>\n   807\t\n   808\tFull reports at:\n   809\t- mission/validations/adversarial-a.md\n   810\t- mission/validations/adversarial-b.md\n   811\t\n   812\tReview the PR and the adversarial findings. You decide what to address.\n   813\tIf you decide not to ship this mission (reviewers found blockers, priorities changed), close the draft PR and the PRD issue yourself: `gh pr close <PR number> --delete-branch` and `gh issue close <PRD issue number> --reason \"not planned\"`. Stop here -- do not proceed to the After merge steps below. The orchestrator only handles the happy path and circuit-breaker abort.\n   814\tAfter merge:\n   815\t1. Run /opsx:archive to move the change files to the archive directory\n   816\t2. Commit and push the archive move:\n   817\t   - If main is unprotected: `git checkout main && git pull && git add openspec/ && git commit -m \"chore: archive <change-name>\" && git push`\n   818\t   - If main is protected: create a branch (`git checkout -b archive/<change-name>`), commit, push, open a PR, merge it\n   819\t```\n   820\t\n   821\tUpdate plan status to COMPLETE.\n   822\t\n   823\t**Gate -- mission is COMPLETE when:**\n   824\t- [ ] Final gates passed (build, test, lint, format)\n   825\t- [ ] Spec delta check clean (no unresolved discrepancies)\n   826\t- [ ] Draft PR created\n   827\t- [ ] Both adversarial reviews complete and presented to human\n   828\t- [ ] Plan status = COMPLETE\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
