{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba skills/mission/templates/plan.md | sed -n '1,80p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Mission: <change-name>\n     2\t\n     3\t## Status: PLANNING | APPROVED | BUILDING | COMPLETE | PAUSED\n     4\t\n     5\t## State Directory\n     6\topenspec/changes/<change-name>/mission/\n     7\t\n     8\t## Darkfactory SHA\n     9\t<full SHA of ~/.darkfactory at plan-creation time; append \"-dirty\" if working tree has uncommitted changes>\n    10\tCaptured so this mission can be reproduced against the exact skill version that ran it.\n    11\t\n    12\t## OpenSpec Artifacts\n    13\t- Proposal: openspec/changes/<change-name>/proposal.md\n    14\t- Specs: openspec/changes/<change-name>/specs/<capability>/spec.md (one per capability)\n    15\t- Design: openspec/changes/<change-name>/design.md\n    16\t- Tasks: openspec/changes/<change-name>/tasks.md (includes mandatory closing tasks)\n    17\t- Coverage Audit: openspec/changes/<change-name>/coverage-audit.md\n    18\t- Contract: openspec/changes/<change-name>/contract.md\n    19\t\n    20\t## Spec Coverage Audit\n    21\t- PRD issue: <GitHub issue URL from Phase 3>\n    22\t- PRD issue number: <N>\n    23\t- Coverage table: <pending | complete>\n    24\t- Gaps found: <count or \"none\">\n    25\t- Gaps resolved: <added N tasks | deferred N | skipped N>\n    26\t\n    27\t## Engine Config\n    28\tDefaults defined in Phase 6 config.yaml. \n    29\t\n    30\t## Skills to Use\n    31\t- /grill -- alignment interview (planning)\n    32\t- /language -- shared language (planning)\n    33\t- /prd -- structured PRD from grill conversation (planning)\n    34\t- openspec CLI -- create artifacts sequentially: proposal, specs, design, tasks (planning)\n    35\t- /review -- code review (scrutiny validation)\n    36\t- /simplify -- simplify pass (scrutiny validation)\n    37\t- /security -- security check (scrutiny validation, sensitive tasks only)\n    38\t- /tdd -- test-driven development for workers (build phase)\n    39\t- /test-app -- browser tests (user-test validation)\n    40\t- /demo-video -- frontend demo recording (post-validation)\n    41\t- gh pr create --draft (completion, no skill needed)\n    42\t- /opsx:archive -- archive change (post-merge)\n    43\t\n    44\t## Mission Flow\n    45\tFor each unchecked task in tasks.md (skip `- [~]` tasks):\n    46\t1. Read mission state from progress.md\n    47\t2. Write brief to mission/briefs/task-N.md\n    48\t3. Dispatch worker (engine from config.yaml)\n    49\t4. Read handoff from mission/handoffs/task-N.md\n    50\t5. Spawn scrutiny validator (commit SHA + contract assertions)\n    51\t6. If fail -> write to issues/, spawn fix worker, re-validate. Circuit breaker at 3.\n    52\t7. Spawn user-test validator (commit SHA + contract assertions)\n    53\t8. If fail -> same fix/re-validate loop\n    54\t9. If frontend task -> spawn demo video\n    55\t10. Mark task done in tasks.md, update progress.md\n    56\t\n    57\tAfter all tasks complete:\n    58\t11. Run final gates (build, test, lint, format)\n    59\t12. Run spec delta check against coverage audit\n    60\t13. Create draft PR\n    61\t14. Run dual adversarial review (Codex + Claude): each walks mission commits one at a time, groups findings by task, then does a cross-task pass\n    62\t15. Present both reports to human alongside PR link\n    63\t\n    64\t## Rules\n    65\t- One worker at a time (serial execution)\n    66\t- Workers never see contract.md\n    67\t- Validators never see proposal.md or design.md\n    68\t- On any failure, re-run both per-task validators after fix (scrutiny, user-test)\n    69\t- Write all decisions to progress.md\n    70\t\n    71\t## Codebase Deltas\n    72\t<Accumulated after each task passes validation. Used to populate \"What Previous Tasks Built\" in subsequent briefs. Generated from git diff, never from handoff reports.>\n    73\t\n    74\t## Current Task: <N or \"none\">\n    75\t## Current Step: <step name or \"none\">\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
